==French==

===Etymology===
{{rfscript|Gothic}} 
{{etyl|frm|fr}} {{term|toucher|toucher, touchier|lang=frm}} from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{term|tochier|||lang=fro}} (compare {{fr}} doublet {{term|toquer|||lang=fr}} "to offend"), from unattested {{etyl|VL.|fr}} *{{term||toccare||lang=la}} "to knock, strike, offend", of {{etyl|gem|fr}} origin, from Low {{etyl|frk|fr}} *{{term||tokkōn, *tukkōn|to touch|lang=frk}}, from {{proto|Germanic|tukkojanan||tukkianan|to jerk, knock, strike, offend|lang=fr}}, influenced by proximity to similar forms from {{proto|Germanic|tek-||tēk-|to touch|lang=fr}}. Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|zochhon|zochhōn||lang=goh}} "to grasp, seize", {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|zuchon|zuchôn||lang=goh}} "to jerk, tug", {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|tucken|tucken||lang=gmh}} "to tug", {{etyl|odt|-}} {{term|tocken|tocken, tucken||lang=odt}} "to touch, entise", {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|tucian|tucian, tūcian||lang=ang}} "to mistreat, disturb, torment", {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|tekan|tekan||lang=}} "to touch", {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|taka|taka||lang=non}} "to touch, grasp", {{ang}} {{term|tacan|tacan||lang=ang}} "to touch, take".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tu.ʃe/|lang=fr}}, {{X-SAMPA|/tu.Se/}}
* {{audio|Fr-toucher.ogg|Audio (France, Paris)}}
* {{rhymes|e|lang=fr}}
* {{exthomophones|touchai|touché|touchée|touchées|touchers|touchés|touchez|lang=fr}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m}}

# The act of [[touching]] {{i|see below}}.
# A way of touching.
# The [[sensorial function]] [[touch]].

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# {{transitive|lang=fr}} To [[touch]] (physically).
#: ''Ne me '''touche''' pas !''
#:: ''Don't touch me!''
# {{transitive|lang=fr}} To [[move]] (emotionally)
# To [[affect]]
#: ''La maladie touche actuellement 2 millions de personnes.''
#:: ''The disease currently affects 2 million people.''
# {{intransitive|followed by "[[à#French|à]]"|lang=fr}} To [[try]], to [[try out]].
#: ''Je n'ai jamais '''touché''' au tabac''
#:: ''I've never tried tobacco''

